### Colonial Empire JE widget — the player-facing surface for je_colonial_empire,
### laid out to docs/guides/gui_style_guide.md.
###
### Three roots at the foot of this file, all mounted from je_colonial_empire:
###   widget_je_colonial_empire_overview   custom_widget_container_1
###       the overview (te_ce_overview_panel), always shown: the band, the
###       programmes running, the stability bar with the next band marked, and
###       the condemning great powers' share of prestige.
###   widget_je_colonial_empire_status     custom_widget_container_2
###       te_ce_status_sections, open: why stability is moving, international
###       pressure, the three colonial programmes, the three decolonization
###       decisions.
###   widget_je_colonial_empire_reference  custom_widget_container_3
###       te_ce_reference_sections: the two history charts, then "How the
###       Colonial Empire Works", the one collapsed section of explanations.
### The overview draws the stability bar, so the entry also attaches
### te_je_bars_on_top_marker to custom_widget_container_7 and the journal panel
### drops its own bar at the bottom (gui/journal_entry.gui; je_banking.txt).
###
### Every section is a type (te_ce_sec_*) and the two composers set their order,
### so a system tab can instance the same pieces later (style rule 9). The
### roots are thin wrappers that repeat the composers' IsActive gate.
###
### Collapse flags say their default: *_closed sections are open until closed,
### *_open ones collapsed until opened (test_colonial_empire_layout.py).
###
### The vanilla button grid is AI-only (`is_ai = yes` on all nine buttons), so
### every action a human could take has a control here. Each control calls the
### SAME shared trigger/effect the button calls, through
### common/scripted_guis/colonial_empire_sguis.txt.
###
### OP TABLE — colonial_empire_policy_sgui
###   0  enable  Development Investment      1  disable Development Investment
###   2  enable  Military Garrison           3  disable Military Garrison
###   4  enable  Cultural Assimilation       5  disable Cultural Assimilation
###
### OP TABLE — colonial_empire_decision_sgui
###   0  Release a Colonial Territory   1  Planned Full Decolonization
###   2  Round Table Conference
###
### Both tables are repeated in the sgui file and in
### docs/systems/journal_entry_systems.md § Colonial Stability Widget. Keep all
### three in step.
###
### An op code decides what a control DOES, never whether it is DRAWN. Each
### programme's Enable/Disable pair takes its visibility from a scope-free
### read-only handler — colonial_empire_active_{invest,garrison,assimilation}_sgui
### — with Disable on `IsShown(...)` and Enable on `Not(IsShown(...))`. The
### overview's lit and dimmed programme icons read the same three handlers.
### Passing a saved scope to IsValid / Execute / the tooltips is proven in this
### mod; passing one to IsShown is not, and with the button grid hidden from
### humans a row whose visibility quietly evaluated false would leave no control
### at all. The sgui file header has the full reasoning. Do not move visibility
### onto an op-parameterised IsShown.
###
### NO NUMBER IS TYPED IN THIS FILE. The nine stability contributions come from
### colonial_stability_drift_* script values — the same leaves the bar itself
### consumes — six read live and three read from the snapshot variables
### colonial_empire_refresh_display writes. The band and the next band's edge
### come from the live band ladder (colonial_empire_live_tier /
### colonial_empire_live_next_boundary in colonial_empire_values.txt), never
### from the snapshot, which is stale on a newly activated entry; the overview
### reads them and its snapshots through the guarded colonial_empire_disp_*
### values.
### Programme costs and effects come from [GetStaticModifier('x').GetDesc]. If
### you need a new number here, derive it in colonial_empire_display_effects.txt
### and read the variable.
###
### je_colonial_empire carries `is_shown_when_inactive`, so every root is gated
### on [JournalEntry.IsActive] (gotcha #14: an unguarded display sgui in that
### state produces a "Failed to fetch variable" per frame for every country that
### can merely see the entry). Inside, every var read is additionally gated on
### colonial_empire_display_ready, which asks script whether
### colonial_empire_refresh_display has run yet.
###
### Section open/closed state and the chart range live in GetVariableSystem —
### client-side UI state, never saved, never gameplay state. There is no armed
### action state anywhere: the three decolonization decisions confirm through
### decolonization_events.400 / .401, which is real game state and offers a
### Reconsider option.
###
### Placeholder art: the band, alert and programme icons and the pie's fill are
### vanilla textures standing in for the system's own icons. Each is listed,
### with what the final art should show, in docs/systems/colonial_empire_gui_icons.md.

types colonial_empire_widget_types
{
	type colonial_empire_text = textbox {
		autoresize = yes
		multiline = yes
		minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
		maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
		align = left|nobaseline
		using = fontsize_large
	}

	type colonial_empire_panel = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		parentanchor = hcenter
		margin = { 20 8 }

		background = {
			using = entry_bg_fancy_dark
			alpha = 0.5
		}
	}

	type colonial_empire_section_header = section_header_button {
		blockoverride "layout" {
			parentanchor = hcenter
			size = { 520 38 }
		}
		blockoverride "left_text_alignment" {
			align = left|nobaseline
		}
	}

	### A heading inside a section's panel, over one group of its lines, with a
	### faint rule under it (un_chamber_subheader's shape).
	type colonial_empire_subheader = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 1
		block "subheader_margin" {
			margin_top = 10
		}

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			multiline = yes
			maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_large
			default_format = "#title"
			block "subheader_text" {}
		}
		divider_clean = {
			blockoverride "size" {
				size = { 480 2 }
			}
		}
	}

	### Explanatory text under a subheading in "How the Colonial Empire Works":
	### how a part of the system works, rather than what it says now.
	type colonial_empire_note = textbox {
		autoresize = yes
		multiline = yes
		minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
		maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
		align = left|nobaseline
		using = fontsize_medium
		default_format = "#lore"
	}

	### A table row: a label on the left and its value on the right
	### (un_chamber_value_row's shape). Every row carries a tooltip with the
	### reason behind its value, so the label is marked hoverable.
	type colonial_empire_value_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		margin = { 4 1 }

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 320 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 320 -1 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			elide = right
			block "row_label" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 140 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 140 -1 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			default_format = "#v"
			elide = right
			block "row_value" {}
		}
	}

	### `action_binding` carries the four properties that address the scripted
	### GUI — visible / enabled / onclick / tooltip — because they are the only
	### part that differs between one control and the next.
	type colonial_empire_action_button = button {
		using = default_button_action
		size = { 110 30 }
		parentanchor = vcenter

		textbox = {
			parentanchor = center
			align = center|nobaseline
			autoresize = yes
			max_width = 100
			elide = right
			using = fontsize_small
			block "action_label" {}
		}

		block "action_binding" {}
	}

	### One programme: its name and cost on the left, and an Enable or a Disable
	### control on the right. Exactly one of the two is ever shown, because their
	### scripted GUIs mirror the enable/disable scripted_button pair's `visible`
	### triggers. The datacontext lives on each blockoverride rather than on the
	### type, because the two controls address different op codes of the same
	### scripted GUI.
	type colonial_empire_policy_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 6
		margin = { 4 4 }
		parentanchor = hcenter

		flowcontainer = {
			direction = vertical
			ignoreinvisible = yes
			parentanchor = vcenter
			minimumsize = { 350 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 350 -1 }

			textbox = {
				autoresize = yes
				multiline = yes
				minimumsize = { 350 -1 }
				maximumsize = { 350 -1 }
				align = left|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_medium
				block "row_label" {}
			}
			textbox = {
				autoresize = yes
				multiline = yes
				minimumsize = { 350 -1 }
				maximumsize = { 350 -1 }
				align = left|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_small
				block "row_cost" {}
			}
		}

		colonial_empire_action_button = {
			blockoverride "action_label" {
				text = "je_colonial_empire_btn_enable"
			}
			block "enable_action" {}
		}

		colonial_empire_action_button = {
			blockoverride "action_label" {
				text = "je_colonial_empire_btn_disable"
			}
			block "disable_action" {}
		}
	}

	### One decolonization decision: its name on the left, what it does on
	### hover, and the control that opens its confirmation event beside it
	### (style rule 6; it used to sit under a paragraph, flush left). Every row
	### shares one scripted GUI and differs only by op code, so the datacontext
	### lives here.
	type colonial_empire_decision_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 10
		margin = { 4 4 }
		datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_decision_sgui')]"

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			multiline = yes
			minimumsize = { 300 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 300 -1 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			block "row_text" {}
		}

		button = {
			using = default_button_action
			size = { 150 28 }
			parentanchor = vcenter

			textbox = {
				parentanchor = center
				align = center|nobaseline
				autoresize = yes
				max_width = 140
				elide = right
				using = fontsize_small
				text = "je_colonial_empire_btn_open_choice"
			}

			block "row_action" {}
		}
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### OVERVIEW. Always shown, not collapsible (style rule 1).
	### ======================================================================

	### A cell of the overview: an icon, its word small beneath. Fixed width,
	### so a long word cannot push the row wider (te_un_ov_icon_label's shape).
	type te_ce_ov_icon_label = widget {
		size = { 110 58 }

		icon = {
			size = { 36 36 }
			parentanchor = top|hcenter
			block "icon_texture" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			parentanchor = bottom|hcenter
			autoresize = yes
			max_width = 108
			elide = right
			align = hcenter|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_small
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			block "label" {}
		}
	}

	### One programme: full colour while it runs, dimmed while it does not. The
	### instance sets the texture on both icons, and the visible gate and
	### tooltip on each (te_un_ov_agency's shape).
	type te_ce_ov_programme = widget {
		size = { 40 40 }

		icon = {
			size = { 36 36 }
			parentanchor = center
			block "lit" {}
			block "programme_texture" {}
		}
		icon = {
			size = { 36 36 }
			parentanchor = center
			alpha = 0.25
			block "unlit" {}
			block "programme_texture" {}
		}
	}

	### A 0..1 share as a pie over a background disc, inside vanilla's
	### decorated round frame, its label beneath (te_un_ov_pie's shape; the
	### recipe is "Pie charts of script-held data" in gui_modding_guide.md).
	### Frame 1 of each texture is transparent, frame 2 the colour.
	type te_ce_ov_pie = widget {
		size = { 150 108 }

		icon = {
			size = { 86 86 }
			parentanchor = top|hcenter
			texture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/round_frame_dec.dds"
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 62 62 }
			parentanchor = top|hcenter
			position = { 0 12 }

			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				value = 1
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/un_icons/pie_rest.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				block "pie_value" {}
				texture = "gfx/interface/journal_entry_widgets/ch_model_pie/ch_pie_communist.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
		}
		textbox = {
			parentanchor = bottom|hcenter
			autoresize = yes
			align = hcenter|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			block "label" {}
		}
	}

	### What a returning player checks: which band, which programmes are
	### running, where the bar is and which way it is moving, and how much of
	### the great powers' weight is condemning us.
	type te_ce_overview_panel = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"

		colonial_empire_panel = {
			spacing = 10

			### Before the first monthly assessment (a save upgraded mid-entry):
			### one line in place of the rows that read the snapshot.
			colonial_empire_text = {
				visible = "[Not(GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_display_ready').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End ))]"
				text = "je_colonial_empire_conditions_pending"
			}

			### Row 1: the band · the programmes running
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = horizontal
				spacing = 6
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				parentanchor = hcenter

				### The band. Its tooltip is the entry's status line and the
				### modifier the band puts on the entry (the panel's old "While in
				### this band" line).
				flowcontainer = {
					ignoreinvisible = yes
					visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_display_ready').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_band_tt"

					te_ce_ov_icon_label = {
						visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_tier'), '(CFixedPoint)5' )]"
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/state_status_icons/state_homelands.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							text = "je_colonial_empire_band_solidified"
						}
					}
					te_ce_ov_icon_label = {
						visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_tier'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/state_status_icons/incorporated_state.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							text = "je_colonial_empire_band_stable"
						}
					}
					te_ce_ov_icon_label = {
						visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_tier'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/warning.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							text = "je_colonial_empire_band_strained"
						}
					}
					te_ce_ov_icon_label = {
						visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_tier'), '(CFixedPoint)2' )]"
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/state_status_icons/has_turmoil.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							text = "je_colonial_empire_band_crumbling"
						}
					}
					te_ce_ov_icon_label = {
						visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_tier'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/war_goals/independence.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							text = "je_colonial_empire_band_collapsing"
						}
					}
				}

				### The three programmes, lit while they run. Which half of each
				### pair is drawn comes from the same scope-free handlers that pick
				### the Enable or the Disable control below.
				widget = {
					size = { 150 58 }

					flowcontainer = {
						direction = horizontal
						spacing = 4
						parentanchor = top|hcenter

						te_ce_ov_programme = {
							blockoverride "programme_texture" {
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/building_icons/building_browser_filter_icons/filter_icons_development.dds"
							}
							blockoverride "lit" {
								visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_active_invest_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
								tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_invest_on_tt"
							}
							blockoverride "unlit" {
								visible = "[Not(GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_active_invest_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End ))]"
								tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_invest_off_tt"
							}
						}
						te_ce_ov_programme = {
							blockoverride "programme_texture" {
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/battalions.dds"
							}
							blockoverride "lit" {
								visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_active_garrison_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
								tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_garrison_on_tt"
							}
							blockoverride "unlit" {
								visible = "[Not(GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_active_garrison_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End ))]"
								tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_garrison_off_tt"
							}
						}
						te_ce_ov_programme = {
							blockoverride "programme_texture" {
								texture = "gfx/interface/population/pop_culture.dds"
							}
							blockoverride "lit" {
								visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_active_assimilation_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
								tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_assimilation_on_tt"
							}
							blockoverride "unlit" {
								visible = "[Not(GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_active_assimilation_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End ))]"
								tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_assimilation_off_tt"
							}
						}
					}
					textbox = {
						parentanchor = bottom|hcenter
						autoresize = yes
						align = hcenter|nobaseline
						using = fontsize_small
						text = "je_colonial_empire_ov_programmes_label"
					}
				}
			}

			### Row 2: the stability bar, a marker where the next band begins,
			### the value and this month's projected change, and its direction.
			### Reached the way vanilla's journal panel reaches it, through the
			### entry's own datamodel (one scripted bar, so one item). The row's
			### tooltip is the engine's own term-by-term breakdown, which reads
			### only the ScriptedProgressBar (gotcha #24: a tooltip in a datamodel
			### item has no JournalEntry). Everything else in the row is a widget
			### property or text, which does see JournalEntry.
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = vertical
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				parentanchor = hcenter
				datamodel = "[JournalEntry.GetScriptedProgressBars]"

				item = {
					flowcontainer = {
						direction = horizontal
						spacing = 8
						ignoreinvisible = yes
						tooltip = "[ScriptedProgressBar.GetPeriodicProgressBreakdown]"

						textbox = {
							minimumsize = { 90 -1 }
							maximumsize = { 90 -1 }
							autoresize = yes
							parentanchor = vcenter
							align = left|nobaseline
							text = "je_colonial_empire_ov_stability_label"
						}
						default_progressbar_horizontal = {
							size = { 200 18 }
							parentanchor = vcenter
							blockoverride "values" {
								value = "[JournalEntry.GetCurrentBarProgress(ScriptedProgressBar.Self)]"
								min = 0
								max = 1
							}
							### The next band's edge (the marker technique of the UN
							### overview's authority target).
							blockoverride "on_top_of_the_progressbar" {
								progressbar = {
									visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_display_ready').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
									noprogresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
									progresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
									size = { 100% 100% }
									skip_initial_animation = yes
									direction = horizontal
									value = "[FixedPointToFloat( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_next_boundary_frac') )]"
									min = 0
									max = 1
									marker = {
										icon = {
											size = { 36 20 }
											parentanchor = vcenter
											widgetanchor = center
											texture = "gfx/interface/progressbar/progressbar_marker.dds"
										}
									}
								}
							}
						}
						textbox = {
							minimumsize = { 120 -1 }
							maximumsize = { 120 -1 }
							autoresize = yes
							parentanchor = vcenter
							align = left|nobaseline
							elide = right
							text = "je_colonial_empire_ov_stability_value"
						}
						widget = {
							size = { 24 24 }
							parentanchor = vcenter

							icon = {
								size = { 24 24 }
								visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_trend'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/trend_up.dds"
							}
							icon = {
								size = { 24 24 }
								visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_trend'), '(CFixedPoint)-1' )]"
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/trend_down.dds"
							}
							icon = {
								size = { 24 24 }
								visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_trend'), '(CFixedPoint)0' )]"
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/trend_nochange.dds"
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}

			### Row 3: where the next band begins, under the marker that shows it.
			textbox = {
				visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_display_ready').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
				autoresize = yes
				parentanchor = hcenter
				align = hcenter|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_medium
				text = "je_colonial_empire_ov_next"
			}

			### Row 4: the great powers. The pie is the condemners' share of
			### great-power prestige (ours included), the number the two
			### escalations fire on; its tooltip is International Pressure's
			### roster, built only while hovered. Beside it, the escalation in
			### force, if any.
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = horizontal
				spacing = 6
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				parentanchor = hcenter
				visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_display_ready').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"

				te_ce_ov_pie = {
					tooltip = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_pressure_sgui').ExecuteTooltip(GuiScope.SetRoot(JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope).End)]"
					blockoverride "pie_value" {
						value = "[FixedPointToFloat( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_condemner_share') )]"
					}
					blockoverride "label" {
						text = "je_colonial_empire_ov_pie_label"
					}
				}
				te_ce_ov_icon_label = {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_pressure_level'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
					parentanchor = vcenter
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_isolation_tt"
					blockoverride "icon_texture" {
						texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/disapproval_icon.dds"
					}
					blockoverride "label" {
						text = "je_colonial_empire_ov_isolation"
					}
				}
				te_ce_ov_icon_label = {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_empire_disp_pressure_level'), '(CFixedPoint)2' )]"
					parentanchor = vcenter
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_ov_consensus_tt"
					blockoverride "icon_texture" {
						texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/red_cross.dds"
					}
					blockoverride "label" {
						text = "je_colonial_empire_ov_consensus"
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### SECTIONS. Each is composed, in order, by te_ce_status_sections or
	### te_ce_reference_sections below.
	### ======================================================================

	### Why stability is moving: the nine groups of the bar's formula as a
	### table, then the monthly limit and the total. Open by default (the
	### CLOSED flag). Each row's tooltip says what the group holds; the
	### explanations are in "How the Colonial Empire Works".
	type te_ce_sec_stability = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4

		colonial_empire_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "je_colonial_empire_stability_header"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('colonial_empire_stability_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_stability_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_stability_closed'))]"
			}
		}

		colonial_empire_panel = {
			visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_stability_closed'))]"

			# Shown for a save upgraded mid-entry, until the first pulse.
			colonial_empire_text = {
				visible = "[Not(GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_display_ready').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End ))]"
				text = "je_colonial_empire_conditions_pending"
			}

			# Six groups read live (a click moves them the next frame); the
			# three that iterate — overreach, great-power pressure, acceptance —
			# read this month's snapshot, behind the display_ready gate.
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = vertical
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_display_ready').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"

				colonial_empire_value_row = {
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_drift_base_tt"
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "je_colonial_empire_drift_base"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_stability_drift_base')|=+2]"
					}
				}
				colonial_empire_value_row = {
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_drift_laws_tt"
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "je_colonial_empire_drift_laws"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_stability_drift_laws')|=+2]"
					}
				}
				colonial_empire_value_row = {
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_drift_igs_tt"
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "je_colonial_empire_drift_igs"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_stability_drift_igs')|=+2]"
					}
				}
				colonial_empire_value_row = {
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_drift_rank_tt"
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "je_colonial_empire_drift_rank"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_stability_drift_rank')|=+2]"
					}
				}
				colonial_empire_value_row = {
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_drift_policies_tt"
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "je_colonial_empire_drift_policies"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_stability_drift_policies')|=+2]"
					}
				}
				colonial_empire_value_row = {
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_drift_domestic_tt"
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "je_colonial_empire_drift_domestic"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_stability_drift_domestic')|=+2]"
					}
				}
				colonial_empire_value_row = {
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_drift_overreach_tt"
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "je_colonial_empire_drift_overreach"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('colonial_empire_d_overreach').GetValue|=+2]"
					}
				}
				colonial_empire_value_row = {
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_drift_gp_tt"
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "je_colonial_empire_drift_gp"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('colonial_empire_d_gp').GetValue|=+2]"
					}
				}
				colonial_empire_value_row = {
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_drift_acceptance_tt"
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "je_colonial_empire_drift_acceptance"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('colonial_empire_d_acceptance').GetValue|=+2]"
					}
				}

				divider_clean = {
					blockoverride "size" {
						size = { 480 2 }
					}
				}

				# What the monthly limit takes off, so the rows add up to the total.
				colonial_empire_value_row = {
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_drift_cap_tt"
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "je_colonial_empire_drift_cap"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_stability_drift_cap_display')|=+2]"
					}
				}
				colonial_empire_value_row = {
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_drift_total_tt"
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "je_colonial_empire_drift_total"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('colonial_stability_drift_total_display')|=+2]"
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### International pressure: which great powers condemn or back us. Collapsed
	### by default, AGAINST style rule 1, for the reason it always was: its
	### roster is walked live in script (colonial_empire_pressure_sgui, two
	### every_country walks per frame while it is open), so nothing runs until
	### the player asks. The overview's pie shows the condemners' share, and its
	### tooltip carries this same roster, built only while hovered.
	type te_ce_sec_pressure = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4

		colonial_empire_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "je_colonial_empire_pressure_header"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('colonial_empire_pressure_open')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_pressure_open'))]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_pressure_open')]"
			}
		}

		colonial_empire_panel = {
			visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_pressure_open')]"

			colonial_empire_text = {
				text = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_pressure_sgui').ExecuteTooltip(GuiScope.SetRoot(JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope).End)]"
			}
		}
	}

	### The three colonial programmes, each with its Enable or Disable control
	### beside it. Open by default.
	type te_ce_sec_programmes = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4

		colonial_empire_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "je_colonial_empire_programmes_header"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('colonial_empire_programmes_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_programmes_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_programmes_closed'))]"
			}
		}

		colonial_empire_panel = {
			visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_programmes_closed'))]"

			# Development Investment — op 0 enable / op 1 disable
			colonial_empire_policy_row = {
				tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_tt_invest"
				blockoverride "row_label" {
					text = "je_colonial_empire_row_invest"
				}
				blockoverride "row_cost" {
					text = "je_colonial_empire_cost_invest"
				}
				blockoverride "enable_action" {
					datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_policy_sgui')]"
					# Visibility comes from the scope-free handler, never from an op code
					# reaching an is_shown block (see the sgui file header).
					visible = "[Not(GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_active_invest_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End ))]"
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End ) ) )]"
				}
				blockoverride "disable_action" {
					datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_policy_sgui')]"
					visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_active_invest_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End ) ) )]"
				}
			}

			# Military Garrison — op 2 enable / op 3 disable
			colonial_empire_policy_row = {
				tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_tt_garrison"
				blockoverride "row_label" {
					text = "je_colonial_empire_row_garrison"
				}
				blockoverride "row_cost" {
					text = "je_colonial_empire_cost_garrison"
				}
				blockoverride "enable_action" {
					datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_policy_sgui')]"
					# Visibility comes from the scope-free handler, never from an op code
					# reaching an is_shown block (see the sgui file header).
					visible = "[Not(GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_active_garrison_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End ))]"
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End ) ) )]"
				}
				blockoverride "disable_action" {
					datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_policy_sgui')]"
					visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_active_garrison_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End ) ) )]"
				}
			}

			# Cultural Assimilation — op 4 enable / op 5 disable
			colonial_empire_policy_row = {
				tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_tt_assimilation"
				blockoverride "row_label" {
					text = "je_colonial_empire_row_assimilation"
				}
				blockoverride "row_cost" {
					text = "je_colonial_empire_cost_assimilation"
				}
				blockoverride "enable_action" {
					datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_policy_sgui')]"
					# Visibility comes from the scope-free handler, never from an op code
					# reaching an is_shown block (see the sgui file header).
					visible = "[Not(GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_active_assimilation_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End ))]"
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ).End ) ) )]"
				}
				blockoverride "disable_action" {
					datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_policy_sgui')]"
					visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_active_assimilation_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)5' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)5' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)5' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)5' ) ).End ) ) )]"
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### The three decolonization decisions. Open by default. The candidate
	### counts sit once above the rows, since an empty count greys all three
	### (style rule 6); each decision's description is on its name's hover.
	type te_ce_sec_decisions = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4

		colonial_empire_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "je_colonial_empire_decisions_header"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('colonial_empire_decisions_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_decisions_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_decisions_closed'))]"
			}
		}

		colonial_empire_panel = {
			visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_decisions_closed'))]"

			# How many territories are on the table, and which one the confirmation
			# event will offer first. The three-candidate flood-fill itself stays in
			# the button action, on click.
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = vertical
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_display_ready').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"

				colonial_empire_value_row = {
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_candidates_eligible_tt"
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "je_colonial_empire_candidates_eligible"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('colonial_empire_eligible_count').GetValue|0]"
					}
				}
				colonial_empire_value_row = {
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_candidates_round_table_tt"
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "je_colonial_empire_candidates_round_table"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('colonial_empire_round_table_count').GetValue|0]"
					}
				}
				# Its own gate: refresh_display removes the variable when nothing
				# qualifies, so this row must not rely on the display_ready gate
				# above alone.
				colonial_empire_value_row = {
					visible = "[GetScriptedGui('colonial_empire_has_candidates').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_candidates_largest_tt"
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "je_colonial_empire_candidates_largest"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('colonial_empire_largest_eligible_state').GetState.GetName]"
					}
				}
			}

			# Release a Colonial Territory — op 0
			colonial_empire_decision_row = {
				blockoverride "row_text" {
					text = "je_colonial_empire_decision_release"
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_decision_release_tt"
				}
				blockoverride "row_action" {
					visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End ) ) )]"
				}
			}

			# Round Table Conference — op 2 (listed second: it is the negotiated
			# middle path between a unilateral grant and liquidating the empire)
			colonial_empire_decision_row = {
				blockoverride "row_text" {
					text = "je_colonial_empire_decision_round_table"
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_decision_round_table_tt"
				}
				blockoverride "row_action" {
					visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End )]"
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End ) ) )]"
				}
			}

			# Planned Full Decolonization — op 1
			colonial_empire_decision_row = {
				blockoverride "row_text" {
					text = "je_colonial_empire_decision_planned"
					tooltip = "je_colonial_empire_decision_planned_tt"
				}
				blockoverride "row_action" {
					visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End ) ) )]"
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### The history charts. Open by default, as the UN's is (the owner's call
	### for the UN, 2026-09-28; rule 1: what changes month to month is open).
	###
	### te_history_chart / te_history_bar_unsigned / te_history_bar_signed /
	### te_history_range_button are declared in
	### gui/journal_entry_widgets/te_history_chart.gui. Types declared in a .gui
	### file are global once loaded, so they are instanced here without
	### including it. `te_hist_range` is a single global GUI variable shared with
	### every other history chart: changing the range here changes it there too.
	type te_ce_sec_history = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4

		colonial_empire_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "je_colonial_empire_history_header"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('colonial_empire_history_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_history_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_history_closed'))]"
			}
		}

		colonial_empire_panel = {
			visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_history_closed'))]"

			# ---- Range ----
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = horizontal
				spacing = 4
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				parentanchor = hcenter

				te_history_range_button = {
					blockoverride "range_text" {
						text = "te_hist_range_1y"
					}
					blockoverride "range_enabled" {
						enabled = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.HasValue( 'te_hist_range', '1' ))]"
					}
					blockoverride "range_onclick" {
						onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Set( 'te_hist_range', '1' )]"
					}
				}
				te_history_range_button = {
					blockoverride "range_text" {
						text = "te_hist_range_5y"
					}
					blockoverride "range_enabled" {
						enabled = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.HasValue( 'te_hist_range', '5' ))]"
					}
					blockoverride "range_onclick" {
						onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Set( 'te_hist_range', '5' )]"
					}
				}
				te_history_range_button = {
					blockoverride "range_text" {
						text = "te_hist_range_20y"
					}
					blockoverride "range_enabled" {
						enabled = "[Or( GetVariableSystem.HasValue( 'te_hist_range', '1' ), GetVariableSystem.HasValue( 'te_hist_range', '5' ) )]"
					}
					blockoverride "range_onclick" {
						onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Set( 'te_hist_range', '20' )]"
					}
				}
			}

			textbox = {
				visible = "[Not( IsDataModelEmpty( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.GetList('te_hist') ) )]"
				parentanchor = hcenter
				autoresize = yes
				multiline = yes
				max_width = 480
				align = hcenter|nobaseline
				text = "te_hist_since"
			}

			# ---- Colonial stability, 0-100 ----
			# Sampled to the nearest 5 (see colonial_empire_refresh_display: the bar
			# is trigger-only, so a comparison ladder is the only read). The legend
			# says so.
			te_history_chart = {
				blockoverride "chart_title" {
					text = "te_hist_chart_colonial_stability_title"
				}
				blockoverride "chart_legend" {
					text = "te_hist_chart_colonial_stability_legend"
				}
				# This series records no markers; the store's pips belong to
				# other systems (banking, cultural hegemony) and would go unexplained.
				blockoverride "marker_pips" {}
				blockoverride "bar_tooltip" {
					tooltip = "te_hist_tt_colonial_stability"
				}
				blockoverride "bar_body" {
					te_history_bar_unsigned = {
						visible = "[ScriptContainer.HasVariable( 'te_hist_v_colonial_stability' )]"
						blockoverride "values" {
							min = 0
							max = 100
							value = "[FixedPointToFloat( Max_CFixedPoint( '(CFixedPoint)2', ScriptContainer.GetVariableValue( 'te_hist_v_colonial_stability' ) ) )]"
						}
						blockoverride "cover_values" {
							min = 0
							max = 100
							value = "[FixedPointToFloat( Max_CFixedPoint( '(CFixedPoint)0', Subtract_CFixedPoint( ScriptContainer.GetVariableValue( 'te_hist_v_colonial_stability' ), '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ) )]"
						}
						blockoverride "color" {
							color = { 0.45 0.68 0.45 1.0 }
						}
					}
				}
			}

			# ---- Projected monthly drift, signed ----
			# Exact: colonial_stability_drift_total, the same capped sum of leaf
			# script values the bar applies. The scale is +/-2 because that sum is
			# capped at +/-colonial_stability_drift_cap (1.667); the cap stripe is
			# 0.17, the same 1/12 of the half-height the other signed charts use.
			te_history_chart = {
				blockoverride "chart_title" {
					text = "te_hist_chart_colonial_drift_title"
				}
				blockoverride "chart_legend" {
					text = "te_hist_chart_colonial_drift_legend"
				}
				# This series records no markers; the store's pips belong to
				# other systems (banking, cultural hegemony) and would go unexplained.
				blockoverride "marker_pips" {}
				blockoverride "zero_axis" {
					widget = {
						size = { 100% 2 }
						parentanchor = vcenter
						alwaystransparent = yes

						background = {
							using = dark_area
							alpha = 0.7
						}
					}
				}
				blockoverride "bar_tooltip" {
					tooltip = "te_hist_tt_colonial_drift"
				}
				blockoverride "bar_body" {
					te_history_bar_signed = {
						visible = "[ScriptContainer.HasVariable( 'te_hist_v_colonial_drift' )]"
						blockoverride "positive_values" {
							min = 0
							max = 2
							value = "[FixedPointToFloat( Max_CFixedPoint( '(CFixedPoint)0', ScriptContainer.GetVariableValue( 'te_hist_v_colonial_drift' ) ) )]"
						}
						blockoverride "positive_cover_values" {
							min = 0
							max = 2
							value = "[FixedPointToFloat( Max_CFixedPoint( '(CFixedPoint)0', Subtract_CFixedPoint( ScriptContainer.GetVariableValue( 'te_hist_v_colonial_drift' ), '(CFixedPoint)0.17' ) ) )]"
						}
						blockoverride "negative_values" {
							min = -2
							max = 0
							value = "[FixedPointToFloat( Min_CFixedPoint( '(CFixedPoint)0', ScriptContainer.GetVariableValue( 'te_hist_v_colonial_drift' ) ) )]"
						}
						blockoverride "negative_cover_values" {
							min = -2
							max = 0
							value = "[FixedPointToFloat( Min_CFixedPoint( '(CFixedPoint)0', Add_CFixedPoint( ScriptContainer.GetVariableValue( 'te_hist_v_colonial_drift' ), '(CFixedPoint)0.17' ) ) )]"
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### "How the Colonial Empire Works": every explanation, gathered out of the
	### live sections into one section at the foot, collapsed by default, one
	### subheading per topic (style rule 1). The live sections say what is
	### happening; this says how it works.
	type te_ce_sec_how = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4

		colonial_empire_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "je_colonial_empire_how_header"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('colonial_empire_how_open')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_how_open'))]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_how_open')]"
			}
		}

		colonial_empire_panel = {
			visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('colonial_empire_how_open')]"

			colonial_empire_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_margin" {}
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "je_colonial_empire_how_sub_bar"
				}
			}
			colonial_empire_note = {
				text = "je_colonial_empire_how_bar_1"
			}
			colonial_empire_note = {
				text = "je_colonial_empire_how_bar_2"
			}
			colonial_empire_note = {
				text = "je_colonial_empire_how_bar_3"
			}
			colonial_empire_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "je_colonial_empire_how_sub_moves"
				}
			}
			colonial_empire_note = {
				text = "je_colonial_empire_how_moves"
			}
			colonial_empire_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "je_colonial_empire_how_sub_pressure"
				}
			}
			colonial_empire_note = {
				text = "je_colonial_empire_how_pressure"
			}
			colonial_empire_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "je_colonial_empire_how_sub_programmes"
				}
			}
			colonial_empire_note = {
				text = "je_colonial_empire_how_programmes"
			}
			colonial_empire_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "je_colonial_empire_how_sub_decolonization"
				}
			}
			colonial_empire_note = {
				text = "je_colonial_empire_how_decolonization"
			}
		}
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### LAYOUT. The one order of the sections.
	### ======================================================================

	### Everything a returning player checks or acts on, open by default
	### except International Pressure (see te_ce_sec_pressure).
	type te_ce_status_sections = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4
		visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"

		te_ce_sec_stability = {}
		te_ce_sec_pressure = {}
		te_ce_sec_programmes = {}
		te_ce_sec_decisions = {}
	}

	### The charts, then how it all works.
	type te_ce_reference_sections = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4
		visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"

		te_ce_sec_history = {}
		te_ce_sec_how = {}
	}
}


### ==========================================================================
### JOURNAL ENTRY ROOTS (je_colonial_empire.txt). Bare wrappers that repeat the
### composers' IsActive gate, so an inactive entry's containers collapse.
### ==========================================================================
flowcontainer = {
	name = "widget_je_colonial_empire_overview"
	visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"
	parentanchor = hcenter
	ignoreinvisible = yes

	te_ce_overview_panel = {}
}

flowcontainer = {
	name = "widget_je_colonial_empire_status"
	visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"
	parentanchor = hcenter
	ignoreinvisible = yes

	te_ce_status_sections = {}
}

flowcontainer = {
	name = "widget_je_colonial_empire_reference"
	visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"
	parentanchor = hcenter
	ignoreinvisible = yes

	te_ce_reference_sections = {}
}
